WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.409
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:16.099
Today, music: how Studio's music page works, and how I put music on one place with triggers.

5
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.298
Open Audio, then Music.

6
00:00:19.298 --> 00:00:22.659
Every playlist your world can play is here,

7
00:00:22.659 --> 00:00:27.740
and each one is a list of songs plus the rules for when it plays.

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:34.647
This one has a mechanical cue, character creation, so it plays while players build their character.

9
00:00:34.647 --> 00:00:38.034
Cues are fixed moments like combat, travel or dying.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.653
Our new one, Show Night, has mood tags instead: circus, crowd, applause and so on.

11
00:00:43.653 --> 00:00:47.486
When a scene feels like a show, Voyage can pick it by itself.

12
00:00:47.933 --> 00:00:52.464
Songs come from two places: upload your own, or browse Latitude's music.

13
00:00:52.464 --> 00:00:57.372
I picked both of ours from Latitude's library, so there was nothing to upload.

14
00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.794
The easiest win: Voyage's own mood playlists, Calm,

15
00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:05.356
Triumphant and the rest, pick themselves by mood tags alone.

16
00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:10.818
Swap your songs into them and your whole world sounds like you, with nothing else to set up.

17
00:01:12.233 --> 00:01:15.244
For music on one place, you pin it with triggers.

18
00:01:15.244 --> 00:01:19.484
Open Mechanics, then Advanced, then Triggers, and open camp music on.

19
00:01:19.484 --> 00:01:22.311
It fires when the party is at the show's camp.

20
00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.162
And only while the flag camp music is false.

21
00:01:26.162 --> 00:01:31.497
It's recurring, so without the flag it would fire again every single turn at camp.

22
00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:37.576
Its effects: music track set plays Camp Theme, and the flag flips to true.

23
00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.719
Camp music off is the mirror.

24
00:01:39.719 --> 00:01:42.973
The flag is true and the party is anywhere but the camp,

25
00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:45.705
so it clears the music and flips the flag back.

26
00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.088
Walk into camp again and it starts again.

27
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:55.767
Remember: a pinned playlist plays until something clears it, so every start needs a stop.

28
00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.597
And there's only one slot.

29
00:01:57.597 --> 00:02:03.653
A second set replaces the first, and a clear stops whatever is pinned, not just yours.

30
00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:10.263
There's also an examples file with seven playlists and eleven triggers: a city,

31
00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:14.670
a person, an item, a trait, night music, a battle theme and a mood.

32
00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:17.235
Voyage's validator accepts all of them,

33
00:02:17.235 --> 00:02:21.379
and the only warnings are the example names you swap for yours.

34
00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.677
That's music, and that's season two.

35
00:02:25.677 --> 00:02:31.416
Our playlists, triggers and the examples are linked in the description.

36
00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:35.781
Next season, the AI tab: what your world tells the AI.

37
00:02:36.233 --> 00:02:40.181
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

